# Machine-specific config
install.config

# CDK context cache. Every entry is keyed by AWS account, so a clone deploying
# into a different account can never hit the entries cached here; the file
# offers other deployers nothing and only accumulates the author's account id,
# AZ lists and hosted zone ids. CDK's own advice is to commit it, which assumes
# an app with fixed target accounts and a pipeline synthesising it. kiro-flock
# is cloned and deployed into the reader's own account, so that does not apply.
# It was already being stripped by hand before each public release; ignoring it
# makes that structural instead of a step someone has to remember.
# Regenerated automatically on the next synth from live credentials.
cdk.context.json

